
NESTJS - OVERVIEW OF CONCEPTS PRACTICED


1. FIRST STEPS
--------------
- Installed NestJS using Nest CLI
- Created project using nest new
- Understood project folder structure
- Learned main.ts as application entry point
- Understood AppModule bootstrapping process

2. CONTROLLERS
--------------
- Handles incoming HTTP requests
- Defined routes using decorators
  @Get()
  @Post()
  @Put()
  @Delete()
- Used @Param(), @Query(), @Body()
- Returns response to client

Example:
GET /users
POST /users

3. PROVIDERS (SERVICES)
-----------------------
- Contains business logic
- Created using @Injectable()
- Used Dependency Injection
- Reusable across application

Example:
UserController -> UserService

4. MODULES
----------
- Organizes application into features
- Groups controllers and providers
- Used @Module() decorator

Example:
UserModule
ProductModule
AuthModule

5. MIDDLEWARE
-------------
- Executes before controller
- Used for logging
- Used for request processing
- Learned importance of next()

Flow:
Request -> Middleware -> Controller

6. EXCEPTION FILTERS
--------------------
- Handles application errors
- Centralized error handling
- Used built-in HTTP exceptions

Example:
throw new NotFoundException()

7. PIPES
--------
- Validation and transformation
- Used ValidationPipe
- Used ParseIntPipe
- Implemented DTO validation

Example:
@Param('id', ParseIntPipe)

8. GUARDS
---------
- Used for authorization
- Determines whether request can proceed
- Implemented CanActivate interface

Flow:
Request -> Guard -> Controller

Example:
JWT Authentication Guard

9. INTERCEPTORS
---------------
- Executes before and after request
- Used for logging
- Response transformation
- Performance monitoring

Flow:
Before Request
Controller
After Response

10. CUSTOM DECORATORS
---------------------
- Created reusable decorators
- Used createParamDecorator()

Example:
@User()

CORE CONCEPTS LEARNED
=====================

1. DEPENDENCY INJECTION (DI)
----------------------------
- Injected services into controllers
- Reduced tight coupling
- Improved maintainability

Example:
constructor(
 private readonly userService: UserService
) {}

2. INVERSION OF CONTROL (IoC)
-----------------------------
- NestJS framework creates and manages objects
- Framework controls dependency creation

3. DTO (DATA TRANSFER OBJECT)
-----------------------------
- Used for request validation
- Defined request structure
- Combined with ValidationPipe

Example:
CreateUserDto

4. TYPESCRIPT DECORATORS
------------------------
@Controller()
@Module()
@Injectable()
@Get()
@Post()
@Body()
@Param()

